<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Yandabo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1826">1826</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-burmese-war">First Anglo-Burmese War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Yandabo was signed on 24 February 1826 by the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and the Konbaung kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-burmese-war">First Anglo-Burmese War</a>. Burma gave up its claims to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, Manipur, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cachar">Cachar</a> and Jaintia, ceded Arakan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanintharyi-region">Tenasserim</a> to the British, paid an indemnity of one million pounds and accepted a British resident. It began British expansion into Burma and north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
